https://api.github.com/licenses/apache-2.0","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTI="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"has_pull_requests":true,"pull_request_creation_policy":"collaborators_only","topics":["ci","code-coverage","developer-tools","github-actions","lsp","mutation-testing","rust","sarif","static-analysis","test-automation","testing","vscode-extension"],"visibility":"public","forks":0,"open_issues":850,"watchers":0,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":true,"maintain":true,"push":true,"triage":true,"pull":true}},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EffortlessMetrics/ripr-swarm/pulls/5451","html_url":"https://github.com/EffortlessMetrics/ripr-swarm/pull/5451","diff_url":"https://github.com/EffortlessMetrics/ripr-swarm/pull/5451.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/EffortlessMetrics/ripr-swarm/pull/5451.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"## What this does\n\nCalibration joins need more than line identity: a runtime mutant and a static seam sharing one line stay ambiguous without columns (#5336, sequenced after the #5295 importer work).\n\n**Change:** probe shapes carry the parser-owned end byte, seams derive 1-based byte-column span geometry (fail-closed to line-only when derivation refuses), and `repo-exposure-json` 0.4 plus `repo-seams` 0.2 emit additive `column`/`end_line`/`end_column`. Seam IDs exclude spans and are unchanged. `calibrate` parses the span into its static record; join behavior is unchanged.\n\n## Compatibility\n\nAdditive optional fields only; span-less entries omit them and consumers fall back to line-only. `agent verify` requires the current 0.4 envelope, so regenerate snapshots rather than hand-editing versions. Cache versions bumped (1.30/0.36/1.19) for cold recompute; no backfill. Tolerant consumers keep 0.3 fixtures as backward-compat coverage.\n\n## Verification\n\n| Check | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| span emission red control (`repo_seams`) | unpatched missing fields, patched carries |\n| omission pins | seam header goes line to owner, no zero coords |\n| `byte_span_to_lines` units | 1-based byte cols, multibyte, multiline, fail-closed quad |\n| seam ID stability | identical with and without span |\n| calibrate span parse | spanned and line-only records |\n| live `check` + `calibrate` on scratch mutant crate | 0.4 with span 1:37-1:42 for `a + b` (exact), join runs |\n| lib suite | 7932 passed; 5 failed, all reproduced on exact base `b0c9ff3` (repair store identity x3, linked-worktree path, empty-PATH git) |\n| `cli_smoke` owned failures | corpus, first-action route, editor loop, proof control green after bless |\n| goldens | pass, 0 drift |\n| `check-fast` / `precommit` | 14 / 32 gates pass |\n| `clippy`, `fmt` | clean |\n\n## Review map\n\n- `analysis/seams.rs`: `SeamSpan`, `byte_span_to_lines` (fail-closed, line cross-check), `with_span`/`span`, ID exclusion, unit tests.\n- `analysis/syntax/ra.rs`, `analysis/facts/model.rs`: parser-owned `end_byte` producer and field (verbatim range end, never `text.len()`).\n- `analysis/seam_inventory.rs`: wiring with fail-closed fallback to line-only.\n- `output/repo_exposure.rs`, `output/repo_seams.rs`: span-when-present emission, 0.4/0.2 bumps, carry/omit tests.\n- `output/mutation_calibration.rs`: `StaticSeamRecord` span parse plus test (enabler for the containment join).\n- `output/schemas.rs`, `output/render.rs`, `analysis/seam_cache.rs`: version pins with cold-recompute routing.\n- `fixtures/.../unchanged-after-attempt/`: re-blessed chain (before/after via real `check`, verify via real `agent verify`, receipt digest re-pin).\n- `docs/OUTPUT_SCHEMA.md`, `docs/CAPABILITY_MATRIX.md`, `docs/specs/RIPR-SPEC-0021-evidence-record.md`, `CHANGELOG.md`, `.ripr/traceability.toml`: contract, entries, test registration.\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- Importer runtime columns plus the containment join (second half, after #5295 lands); receipt/proof/first-action rendering of spans.\n- #5440 card separator defect (separate owner, filed from this lane's triage).\n\n<!-- devin-review-badge-begin -->\n\n---\n\n<a href=\"https://app.devin.ai/review/effortlessmetrics/ripr-swarm/pull/5451\" target=\"_blank\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://static.devin.ai/assets/gh-devin-review-dark.svg?v=4\"><img src=\"https://static.devin.ai/assets/gh-devin-review-light.svg?v=4\" alt=\"Devin Review\"></picture></a>\n<!-- devin-review-badge-end -->","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EffortlessMetrics/ripr-swarm/issues/5451/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EffortlessMetrics/ripr-swarm/issues/5451/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EffortlessMetrics/ripr-swarm/issues/comments/5979252040","html_url":"https://github.com/EffortlessMetrics/ripr-swarm/issues/5440#issuecomment-5979252040","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EffortlessMetrics/ripr-swarm/issues/5440","id":5979252040,"node_id":"IC_kwDOSiSx0c8AAAABZGQlSA","user":{"login":"EffortlessSteven","id":15812269,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1ODEyMjY5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15812269?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/EffortlessSteven","html_url":"https://github.com/EffortlessSteven","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EffortlessSteven/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EffortlessSteven/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EffortlessSteven/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EffortlessSteven/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EffortlessSteven/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EffortlessSteven/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EffortlessSteven/repos","events_url":"https://